{{Quote|No, no. It's beyond the outer rim. I'd say about twelve parsecs outside the Rishi Maze.|[[Dexter Jettster]], on the location of the planet Kamino|<ref name="Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref>}}
The '''Rishi Maze''',<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> also known as '''Companion Aurek''',<ref name="BMF 28">{{BuildFalconCite|28|Starship Fact File}}</ref> was an irregular<ref name="CL 2016" /> dwarf satellite [[galaxy]]<ref name="AB Update">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> in a close and decaying [[orbit]] around the [[The galaxy|galactic plane]] that was home to the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="CL 2016" /> It was located twelve [[parsec]]s away from the [[planet]] [[Kamino]], toward the galactic north.<ref name="Attack of the Clones" />

The Rishi Maze shared its name with the planet [[Rishi]] in the galaxy's [[Abrion sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Ultimate">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Rishi Station]] on the [[Rishi Moon]] was manned by Republic [[clone trooper]]s to defend Kamino and the cloning facilities of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] from [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] invasion.<ref name="Rookies">{{TCW|Rookies (episode)}}</ref>

